      "why": "pipelined already dominates the merged front (13 of 14 designs) and is the reference for the throughput/latency constraints. I keep a smaller share here to refine the front around the current best (38698 um2) and to confirm the accuracy-vs-area knee, but the main new information should come from pipelined_m. Ranges are kept tight (data_width 14-18, n_iter 12-18, guards 0-2) because the error budget (2^-12) is easily met in this region and larger widths/iters only add area without improving the objective."
