  "rationale": "The spec needs >=32 msps throughput (so only pipelined/pipelined_m qualify, both give 1 result/cycle) and a 0.5 us p99 batch bound for 32 requests per 1 us tick, which forces low latency. The error budget is 2^-12, which is loose enough that data_width ~14-18 with n_iter ~12-18 and small guards suffices; pushing width or iterations higher only costs area. The current best is 38698 um2 (pipelined), but pipelined_m has already produced a smaller feasible point (30165 um2), so the area frontier likely bends toward pipelined_m. I therefore spend 60% of the budget on pipelined_m to map its area/accuracy trade-off and find the true minimum-area point, and 40% on pipelined to refine the already-dominant front and confirm the knee. Both families share the same accuracy-determining parameters, so the search focuses on the area-relevant knobs (m for pipelined_m, and the width/iter/guard trade-off for both)."
