  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "The feasible Pareto front is well-established and robust. The minimum area design (pipelined_m, 29151 um^2) comfortably meets all constraints: throughput 78.8 MSPS >= 32, max_abs_err 2.04e-4 <= 2.44e-4, and the system batch latency bound is met (best seen 0.269 us <= 0.5 us). The front spans a reasonable trade-off space (area 29k-50k um^2, accuracy 12.3-14.2 bits) with no obvious gaps. Since this is the final round, further exploration is unnecessary; the current front provides a solid basis for final selection via the min-area rule."
